        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>RABMAG A</strong> ssyrian Rab-mugi, “chief physician,” “who was attached to the king (Jeremiah 39:3, 13), the title of one of Sennacherib’s officers sent with messages to Hezekiah and the people of Jerusalem (2 Kings 18:17-19:13; Isaiah 36:12-37:13) demanding the surrender of the city. He was accompanied by a “great army;” but his mission was unsuccessful. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
